              → JourneyEndpointColumn(.start): "mappin.circle.fill" + statusSuccess.
  dest:   <Flag red/> {t('driveDetail.destination','Destination')}
            primary = endAddress | coords | (endTs ? noAddress : inProgress)
            time = endTs ? <DateTime value=endTs in="vehicle"/> : t('inProgress')
            batt = {t('battery')}: {endBatteryPct ?? '?'}%
              → JourneyEndpointColumn(.destination): "flag.fill" + statusDanger.
  PARITY QUIRKS reproduced VERBATIM (covenant #5 — no parity shortcuts):
    · coords appear only when lat AND lon are both truthy (non-nil, non-zero) — the
      JS `lat && lon` gate; a 0 coordinate falls through to the text fallback.
    · latitude is NOT abs'd — a southern latitude renders the raw negative value
      ("-33.87°S"); only the longitude is abs'd. (web JourneyDetailsPanel.tsx L31/L49)
    · fmtNumber = locale decimal, fixed 2-digit precision (global precision).
    · start column has NO in-progress branch — its fallback is always "No address data".
